Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user wants to migrate their Hugo site to a new theme while preserving custom shortcodes (specifically sidenote functionality) in a maintainable, theme-independent way. The shortcodes are currently defined in the theme itself, but the user wants them to work with any theme they might switch to in the future.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Hugo static site generator
   - Hugo themes and theme independence
   - Hugo shortcodes
   - CSS asset pipeline in Hugo
   - Hugo Pipes for CSS processing
   - Theme-independent CSS approach using assets/css/custom.css
   - Responsive web design with media queries
   - Viewport-based layouts (desktop vs mobile handling for sidenotes)
   - Playwright browser automation for testing

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **layouts/partials/head.html**
     - Why important: Verified that the theme includes custom CSS files through Hugo Pipes
     - Contains: `{{ with resources.Get "css/custom.css" }}` which processes and includes custom.css

   - **assets/css/custom.css**
     - Why important: Primary implementation file for theme-independent sidenote styles
     - Created/modified with full sidenote implementation
     - Code snippet:
     ```css
     /* Sidenote styles - theme-independent implementation */
     .sidenote {
       float: right;
       clear: right;
       margin-right: -60%;
       width: 50%;
       margin-top: 0.3rem;
       margin-bottom: 0;
       font-size: 1.1rem;
       line-height: 1.3;
       vertical-align: baseline;
       position: relative;
     }

     .sidenote-number {
       counter-increment: sidenote-counter;
     }

     .sidenote-number:after,
     .sidenote:before {
       position: relative;
       vertical-align: baseline;
     }

     .sidenote-number:after {
       content: counter(sidenote-counter);
       font-size: 0.7rem;
       top: -0.5rem;
       left: 0.1rem;
     }

     .sidenote:before {
       content: counter(sidenote-counter) " ";
       font-size: 0.7rem;
       top: -0.5rem;
     }

     blockquote .sidenote,
     blockquote .marginnote {
       margin-right: -82%;
       min-width: 59%;
       text-align: left;
     }

     /* Mobile responsive behavior */
     @media (max-width: 760px) {
       .sidenote,
       .marginnote {
         display: none;
       }
     }

     /* Reset counter for article/body contexts */
     body {
       counter-reset: sidenote-counter;
     }

     article {
       counter-reset: sidenote-counter;
     }
     ```

   - **Screenshots captured**:
